==English==

===Etymology===
From the [[Karst]], a region of modern-day Slovenia typified by such landscape; from {{etyl|de}} {{term|Karst}}, from Serbo-Croat {{term|Kras}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|kärst (''US'') ''or'' käst (''UK'')}}, {{IPA|/kɑrst/ (''US'') ''or'' /kɑːst/ (''UK'')}}, {{SAMPA|/kArst/</tt> (''US'') ''or'' <tt>/kA:st/</tt> (''UK'')<tt>}}
*: {{rhymes|ɑː(r)st}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{geology}} A type of [[land]] [[formation]], usually with many [[cave]]s caused by [[limestone]] being dissolved by [[underground]] [[drainage]].
#* '''1978''', M. M. Sweeting, "The Karst of Kweilin, Southern China," ''The Geographical Journal'', vol. 144, no. 2, p. 200,
#*: In the time available to us on our geomorphological tour we were not able to see the higher and younger '''karsts''' of Kweichow and Yunnan and Kunming.

